WEBVTT

00:01:29.263 --> 00:01:31.575
humans have populated areas in the Arctic

00:01:31.575 --> 00:01:33.804
for thousands of years.

00:01:33.804 --> 00:01:37.483
Life in the Arctic includes organisms living in the ice,

00:01:37.483 --> 00:01:39.456
zooplankton and phytoplankton,

00:01:39.456 --> 00:01:41.041
fish and marine mammals,

00:01:41.041 --> 00:01:41.730
birds,

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:42.367
land animals,

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:42.985
plants,

00:01:42.985 --> 00:01:45.084
and human societies.

00:01:45.084 --> 00:01:47.183
Okay, what about Antarctica?

00:01:47.183 --> 00:01:50.224
Antarctica is Earth's southernmost continent,

00:01:50.224 --> 00:01:52.885
and it contains the geographic South Pole.

00:01:52.885 --> 00:01:55.588
It's the fifth largest continent on the planet

00:01:55.588 --> 00:01:57.836
at nearly twice the size of Australia.

00:01:57.836 --> 00:02:01.335
Almost 98% of Anarctica is covered by ice